# agnspec

A component-oriented Python package for fitting AGN (Active Galactic
Nucleus) optical/UV spectra.

## Design

The package is organized around *physical spectral components* rather
than *fitting steps*:

```
AGNModel
├── Continuum
│   ├── PowerLaw
│   ├── HostGalaxy
│   ├── BalmerContinuum
│   └── FeII
│
├── EmissionLines
│   ├── HbetaComplex
│   ├── HalphaComplex
│   ├── MgIIComplex
│   ├── CIVComplex
│   └── OIIIComplex
│
├── Fitters
│   ├── LeastSquares
│   ├── MCMC
│   └── NestedSampling
│
├── Measurements
├── Plotting
└── Pipeline
```

Every continuum component (`PowerLaw`, `HostGalaxy`, `BalmerContinuum`,
`FeII`) and every line complex (`HbetaComplex`, `HalphaComplex`, ...)
exposes the same small interface:

```python
component.model(wave, *params)       # -> model flux
component.initial_guess(wave, flux)  # -> starting parameter vector
component.bounds()                   # -> (lower, upper)
component.param_names                # or .free_param_names
```

This lets any `Fitter` (`LeastSquares`, `MCMC`, `NestedSampling`)
operate on any component, or on the combined `ContinuumModel` /
`LineComplex` objects, without special-casing.

## Module map

| Module              | Contents                                                        |
|----------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `io.py`              | `read_spectrum`, `save_results`, `load_results`                 |
| `preprocessing.py`   | `to_rest_frame`, `deredden_galactic`, `mask_bad_pixels`, `smooth_spectrum` |
| `continuum.py`       | `PowerLaw`, `HostGalaxy`, `BalmerContinuum`, `FeII`, `ContinuumModel`, `fit_continuum`, `fit_powerlaw`, `fit_host_galaxy`, `fit_feii`, `get_continuum_mask` |
| `emission_lines.py`  | `GaussianComponent`, `LineComplex`, `HbetaComplex`, `HalphaComplex`, `MgIIComplex`, `CIVComplex`, `OIIIComplex`, `fit_gaussian`, `fit_multiple_gaussians`, `extract_region` |
| `fitting.py`         | `Fitter`, `LeastSquares`, `MCMC`, `NestedSampling`, `mcmc_fit`, `FitResult` |
| `measurements.py`    | `equivalent_width`, `line_flux`, `fwhm`, `sigma_velocity`, `velocity_shift`, `line_luminosity`, `virial_blackhole_mass`, `eddington_ratio`, `bolometric_luminosity` |
| `uncertainties.py`   | `bootstrap_errors`, `residual_bootstrap_errors`, `credible_interval`, `propagate_errors` |
| `plotting.py`        | `plot_spectrum`, `plot_continuum_fit`, `plot_line_fit`           |
| `utils.py`           | Constants, `LINE_WAVELENGTHS`, Gaussian helpers, unit conversions |
| `models.py`          | `AGNModel` — the top-level object tying everything together      |
| `pipeline.py`        | `run_pipeline` — the full read -> ... -> save pipeline           |

## Pipeline flow

```
Read spectrum
      |
Preprocess
      |
Correct extinction
      |
Shift to rest frame
      |
Mask bad pixels
      |
Fit continuum
      |
Subtract continuum
      |
Fit emission lines
      |
Measure line properties
      |
Estimate uncertainties
      |
Generate plots
      |
Save outputs
```

## Quick start (procedural)

```python
from agnspec.pipeline import run_pipeline

model, results = run_pipeline(
    filename="spectrum.fits",
    z=0.35,
    ebv=0.02,
    line="Hbeta",
    output_dir="./agnspec_output",
)

print(results["line_measurements"]["hbeta_broad"]["fwhm"])
```

## Quick start (component-oriented / object API)

```python
import numpy as np
from agnspec import io, preprocessing as prep
from agnspec.continuum import PowerLaw, FeII, get_continuum_mask
from agnspec.emission_lines import HbetaComplex
from agnspec.fitting import LeastSquares, MCMC
from agnspec.models import AGNModel

wave, flux, err, hdr = io.read_spectrum("spectrum.fits")
flux = prep.deredden_galactic(wave, flux, ebv=0.02)
wave, flux = prep.to_rest_frame(wave, flux, z=0.35)
good = prep.mask_bad_pixels(wave, flux, err)
wave, flux, err = wave[good], flux[good], (err[good] if err is not None else None)

# Build a model: power law + Fe II continuum, Hbeta+[OIII] emission lines
model = AGNModel(
    continuum_components=[PowerLaw()],
    fitter=LeastSquares(),
)
model.add_line_complex("Hbeta", HbetaComplex(include_oiii=True))

windows = [(4200, 4230), (5080, 5130)]
model.fit_continuum(wave, flux, error=err, continuum_windows=windows)
cont = model.continuum_flux(wave)

line_flux = flux - cont
model.fit_line("Hbeta", wave, line_flux, err)

measurements = model.measure_line("Hbeta")
model.plot_continuum()
model.plot_line("Hbeta", wave, line_flux)
```

To instead fit with full Bayesian MCMC (e.g. for the line complex):

```python
model.fitter = MCMC(n_walkers=32, n_steps=3000, n_burn=500)
model.fit_line("Hbeta", wave, line_flux, err)
```

## Optional dependencies

* `emcee` — required for `fitting.MCMC`
* `dynesty` — required for `fitting.NestedSampling`
* `dust_extinction` — used by `preprocessing.deredden_galactic` for
  accurate Fitzpatrick99/CCM89/O94 extinction curves (a simplified
  analytic CCM89 fallback is used if it's not installed)

Install everything with:

```bash
pip install agnspec[all]
```
